From 2b6c086123bb32cfc47795370a86ebcd47f5a3b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:13:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bugfix: identify server distribution and order Unleashed
 versions

Warn when the connected server identifies itself as OpenAI Codex. Compare
numeric Unleashed versions by release precedence, then build number, so a
bare equal release is older and a higher release stays newer.

Base: rust-v0.160.0 (a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc)
Prerequisite: add-branding-and-build-metadata.patch
TDD: just test -p codex-tui --lib -E test(numeric_unleashed_versions_order_release_before_build)
failed before the ordering fix and passed after it. The newer-unmarked-server
regression separately failed before provider classification was corrected.
Green: just test -p codex-tui --lib -E 'test(update_versions) | test(status::remote_connection)'
21 tests passed with the maintained Rust 1.95.0 toolchain.
